# Build outputs
*.apk
*.idsig

# Keep gradle-wrapper.jar: `./gradlew` cannot run on a fresh clone without it.
# Other jars are third-party tooling and stay out.
*.jar
!mtk-optimizer/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reference material — a third party's files, kept local only.
#
# Everything under reference/ is either someone else's file or derived from
# someone else's binary. Only our own two notes are tracked: README explains the
# folder layout and the rule, LEDGER records which sources were analysed and where
# their features landed. Neither is needed to build or run the app.
/reference/*
!/reference/README.md
!/reference/LEDGER.md

# Android build artifacts (mtk-optimizer sub-project handles its own)
*.iml
.gradle
/.gradle-user/
/.local-baselines/
/.android-sdk/
/.android-user/
.kotlin
build/
captures/
local.properties

# IDE / OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.cursor/

# Claude Code
.claude/
# Skill 安装锁：本地工具状态，不是项目内容。
skills-lock.json

# Python 字节码缓存：检查器的运行产物，不是项目内容。
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# NOTE: every rule above that names a directory is anchored with a leading
# slash for a reason. A bare `src/` also matches `mtk-optimizer/app/src/`, which
# silently keeps the app's own new source files out of the repository while the
# already-tracked ones keep working — so the mistake is invisible until someone
# clones fresh.

# Cloud-sync client temp files. These appear next to a file while it uploads and
# have twice ended up staged — they are not part of the project.
*.uploading.*
*.baiduyun.*
*.onedrive.*
*.dropbox.*
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signing — never commit these.
#
# mtk-optimizer/signing/ holds the release keystore and the property file that carries its
# passwords in clear text. Losing the .jks means losing the ability to ship an
# update users can install over an existing one: a different signature forces
# an uninstall, which wipes their profiles, settings and saved reports. So the
# file itself must be backed up offline, and it must never enter git history
# where a password leak cannot be undone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/mtk-optimizer/signing/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 本地临时文件 —— 调试截图、uiautomator 导出、一次性脚本。不参与构建，
# 也不该进版本库；留着会让 `git status` 每次都被噪声淹没。
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.scratch/
/.workbuddy/
/*.png
/ui*.xml
/ui-nodes.txt
/tapnav.py
/*.stackdump
